  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Isocistanoside C may interact with the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex through a series of molecular targets, all of which are involved in the regulation of gene expression. Specifically, Isocistanoside C is predicted to target Phosphodiesterase 6C, which is known to be a target of several other compounds, including Methyl 9-cyclopropylnonanoate and (+)-Vouacapenic Acid. These compounds, in turn, are predicted to interact with the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex, indicating a potential pathway through which Isocistanoside C may exert its effects. The consistent scores across the three paths suggest a strong, albeit indirect, relationship between Isocistanoside C and the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex, likely mediated through the phosphodiesterase 6C pathway. The evidence supports the hypothesis that Isocistanoside C may modulate gene expression by influencing the activity of the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm this mechanism.",
